{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 bore carries a tight tolerance band of 0.018 mm, but the drawing does not account for the thickness added by the I.Z.B.P. plating; after plating the hole will be undersize and the intended fit will fail. The designer must either open the pre-plate machining limits to leave room for the coating or add a note requiring re-machining/masking of the bore after plating."
    ,
"recommended_correction":"Specify pre-plate machining limits that allow for plating build-up on the H7 bore, or add a note to mask or re-machine the bore after plating."}]}
